        a="Small offices still running an Exchange server in a cupboard are carrying risk: older versions are out of support and have been targeted by serious attacks. For them, Exchange support usually means a planned move to Exchange Online. For businesses already in the cloud, it means permissions, shared calendars, mail rules and the occasional message that never arrived.",
        x="If you still run an on-premises Exchange server, check which version it is. Unsupported versions should be moved or retired as a priority, and we can plan that migration.",
