        a="A NAS is a sensible choice for offices with large files, slow internet or software that needs local storage. Set-up decides how reliable it will be: which disks, how they are arranged, who can see which folders and where the second copy goes. Getting those right at the start avoids the common story of a NAS that quietly fails until the second disk dies.",
